{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals their length using prefix sums.\n    This method leverages the fact that `sum(digits[i:j]) == j - i` is equivalent to\n    `prefix_sum[j] - prefix_sum[i] == j - i`, which simplifies to\n    `prefix_sum[j] - j == prefix_sum[i] - i`.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    prefix_sum = 0\n    # Store frequencies of (prefix_sum - index) values\n    # The key 0 represents the state before processing any digit (prefix_sum=0, index=0).\n    freq = collections.defaultdict(int)\n    freq[0] = 1 \n\n    for idx, char_digit in enumerate(s):\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        prefix_sum += digit\n        \n        # Calculate the key: current_prefix_sum - current_length\n        # Current_length is (idx + 1) because idx is 0-based.\n        key = prefix_sum - (idx + 1)\n        \n        # If this key has been seen before, it means there are substrings ending at 'idx'\n        # with sum of digits equal to their length.\n        count += freq[key]\n        \n        # Increment frequency for the current key\n        freq[key] += 1\n    \n    return count"}
