{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "import operator\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef is_sublist(container: List[Any], sub: List[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list contains the given sublist contiguously.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub:\n        return True # An empty sublist is considered present in any container.\n\n    if len(sub) > len(container):\n        return False # If the sublist is longer, it cannot be found.\n\n    n = len(container)\n    m = len(sub)\n\n    # Iterate through all possible starting positions in the container\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        match = True\n        # Check if the segment of the container matches the sublist\n        for j in range(m):\n            if not operator.eq(container[i + j], sub[j]):\n                match = False\n                break\n        \n        if match:\n            return True # Sublist found\n\n    return False # No match found after checking all positions"}
