{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Sequence\n\ndef _all_divisible(tup: Tuple[int, ...], k: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in a tuple are divisible by k.\n    An empty tuple is considered to have all elements divisible by k.\"\"\"\n    return all(element % k == 0 for element in tup)\n\ndef find_tuples(items: Sequence[Sequence[int]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples from a list where all elements are divisible by k.\n    This function assumes k is a non-zero integer and inner sequences contain only integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    result: List[Tuple[int, ...]] = []\n    for seq in items:\n        current_tuple = tuple(seq) \n        if _all_divisible(current_tuple, k):\n            result.append(current_tuple)\n    return result"}
