{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined as a(1)=1, a(2)=1, a(n)=a(a(n-1))+a(n-a(n-1)) for n>2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        # Based on FR1 and validators.py, n must be >= 1.\n        # However, the prompt explicitly says \"DO NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\"\n        # so I will proceed assuming valid input as per the function contract.\n        pass\n\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        # All values needed for a(i) must already be in memo\n        # because we are calculating iteratively from 1 up to i.\n        val_n_minus_1 = memo[i - 1]\n        term1 = memo[val_n_minus_1]\n        term2 = memo[i - val_n_minus_1]\n        memo[i] = term1 + term2\n\n    return memo[n]"}
