{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of a given non-negative integer n to 1.\n    Raises TypeError for non-int input or ValueError for negative input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be int\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    # Determine bit length to cover n. At least 1 bit is needed for n=0.\n    # The mask will be constructed up to this length.\n    bit_len = max(1, n.bit_length())\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through even bit positions (0, 2, 4, ...) up to bit_len\n    for k in range(0, bit_len, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << k) # Set the k-th bit in the mask to 1\n\n    # Use bitwise OR to set the even bits in n while preserving other bits\n    return n | mask"}
