{"task_id": "Mbpp/418", "solution": "def Find_Max(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element in a list that has the maximum length.\n    If multiple elements have the same maximum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return None  # Or raise an error if an empty list is an invalid input per a strict interpretation\n\n    max_length = -1\n    max_element = None\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        try:\n            current_length = len(element)\n            if current_length > max_length:\n                max_length = current_length\n                max_element = element\n        except TypeError:\n            # Skip elements that do not have a length (e.g., integers, None)\n            continue\n    \n    return max_element"}
