{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "def first_Digit(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first digit of a given number, supporting integers, floats, and numeric strings.\n    Floats are truncated towards zero, and negative signs are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_value = str(value).strip()\n    if '.' in s_value:\n        s_value = s_value.split('.', 1)[0]\n    \n    number_as_int = int(s_value)\n    abs_number = abs(number_as_int)\n    \n    return int(str(abs_number)[0])"}
